    "title": "Allocate CompositeIterator registration storage only when needed"
  },
  "review_statement": "## Problem and change\n\nAn empty CompositeIterator allocated a registration set and its map before use, then allocated an empty traversal array. Create registration storage on the first add and reuse a shared empty traversal array.\n\nKeep the existing nonempty set algorithm, hash/equals and nested-add behavior, freeze lifecycle, child callback order, revived children, and abrupt failures. Preserve the existing source-pinned tests; add ten lifecycle/storage tests. Bring the existing stream-provider contract test into Spring's AssertJ/import/header/format conventions so the required check task can execute.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **Full :spring-core:check passed again on the final notice-complete sources**, including Checkstyle, NullAway, architecture, and multi-release validation.\n- Three source lanes: **16,051 executions, zero failures/errors, 12 existing skip occurrences**. All three lanes use the build's Java 25 launcher.\n- Separate real Java 21 proof: fork candidate **22 tests** and composed M3JDK candidate **17 tests**, each under default and `-Xint`. The exact R2 owners were recompiled against unchanged qualified test/support classes.\n- Changed classes compile with all lint/Werror; public descriptors and method instructions are identical to the pre-notice candidate. Receiving support sources retain three inherited serial warnings.\n\nNonempty registration deliberately retains the current set semantics; this is a bounded allocation improvement rather than a claim that every Spring collection structure is array-backed.\n\n## Canonical execution\n\nCanonical recipe: `com.synexia.m3jdk.CollectionsContractRefinement20261017`, source revision **7af83c5ee4ad166d8cd45c6c33822debabd705ca**, review https://github.com/hsoliwal/com.synexia/pull/15427. Product bytes were emitted by actual qualified SDK Results and the second receive changed zero files. The canonical recipe and executable receiver remain in Synexia.\n",
